IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cbca-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cb1-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part IV, sections 21.1 to 21.4: the register
-- of individuals with significant control (21.1), what a corporation sends and discloses (21.2, 21.21,
-- 21.3), what the Director may give out and must publish (21.301, 21.302, 21.303), requests by
-- investigative bodies (21.31, 21.32) and the offences (21.4). Who is an "individual with significant
-- control" is the keel's definition (s 2.1, cbca-core-isc.l4); here it is a fact about a person.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Each rule is named `<what it decides> within s <section>`. Facts that the Act hands to
-- the regulations ("prescribed"), to the Director ("determined by the Director") or to a judgement
-- ("reasonable steps") are plain inputs. An offence is two rules: whether the person commits it, and the
-- most a court may impose.

§ `Part IV -- Register of individuals with significant control (s 21.1 to s 21.4)`

§§ `s 21.1 the register`

-- s 21.1(1): the register contains, for each individual with significant control, the items in (a)(i)
-- to (a)(iii), (a.1), (b), (c) and (d), any other prescribed information (e) and a description of each step
-- taken under subsection (2) (f). Item (a)(iii) is required only "if it has been provided to the
-- corporation". The register is kept at the registered office or another place in Canada designated by the
-- directors.
-- src:302 | 21.1 (1) The corporation shall prepare and maintain, at its registered office or at any other place in Canada designated by the directors, a register of individuals with significant control over the corporation that contains
-- src:303 | (a) for each individual with significant control,
-- src:304 | (i) their name and date of birth,
-- src:305 | (ii) their residential address, and
-- src:306 | (iii) their address for service, if it has been provided to the corporation;
-- src:307 | (a.1) the citizenship of each individual with significant control;
-- src:308 | (b) the jurisdiction of residence for tax purposes of each individual with significant control;
-- src:309 | (c) the day on which each individual became or ceased to be an individual with significant control, as the case may be;
-- src:310 | (d) a description of how each individual is an individual with significant control over the corporation, including, as applicable, a description of their interests and rights in respect of shares of the corporation;
-- src:311 | (e) any other prescribed information; and
-- src:312 | (f) a description of each step taken in accordance with subsection (2).
@ref CBCA s 21.1(1) register (src:302-312)
DECLARE `Register of individuals with significant control as kept (s 21.1(1))` HAS
    `the register is kept at the registered office or at another place in Canada designated by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it contains the name and date of birth of each individual with significant control` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: who is an individual with significant control is section 2.1 (keel)
    `it contains the residential address of each individual with significant control` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an address for service has been provided to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it contains the address for service of each individual with significant control` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it contains the citizenship of each individual with significant control` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it contains the jurisdiction of residence for tax purposes of each individual with significant control` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it contains the day on which each individual became or ceased to be an individual with significant control` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it contains a description of how each individual is an individual with significant control over the corporation, including a description of their interests and rights in respect of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is other prescribed information` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
    `it contains the other prescribed information` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
    `it contains a description of each step taken in accordance with subsection 21.1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:302 | 21.1 (1) The corporation shall prepare and maintain, at its registered office or at any other place in Canada designated by the directors, a register of individuals with significant control over the corporation that contains
-- src:303 | (a) for each individual with significant control,
-- src:304 | (i) their name and date of birth,
-- src:305 | (ii) their residential address, and
-- src:306 | (iii) their address for service, if it has been provided to the corporation;
-- src:307 | (a.1) the citizenship of each individual with significant control;
-- src:308 | (b) the jurisdiction of residence for tax purposes of each individual with significant control;
-- src:309 | (c) the day on which each individual became or ceased to be an individual with significant control, as the case may be;
-- src:310 | (d) a description of how each individual is an individual with significant control over the corporation, including, as applicable, a description of their interests and rights in respect of shares of the corporation;
-- src:311 | (e) any other prescribed information; and
-- src:312 | (f) a description of each step taken in accordance with subsection (2).
@ref CBCA s 21.1(1) register (src:302-312)
GIVEN register IS A `Register of individuals with significant control as kept (s 21.1(1))`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the register contains what s 21.1(1) requires` MEANS
        register's `the register is kept at the registered office or at another place in Canada designated by the directors`
    AND register's `it contains the name and date of birth of each individual with significant control`
    AND register's `it contains the residential address of each individual with significant control`
    AND (register's `an address for service has been provided to the corporation` IMPLIES register's `it contains the address for service of each individual with significant control`)
    AND register's `it contains the citizenship of each individual with significant control`
    AND register's `it contains the jurisdiction of residence for tax purposes of each individual with significant control`
    AND register's `it contains the day on which each individual became or ceased to be an individual with significant control`
    AND register's `it contains a description of how each individual is an individual with significant control over the corporation, including a description of their interests and rights in respect of shares`
    AND (register's `there is other prescribed information` IMPLIES register's `it contains the other prescribed information`)
    AND register's `it contains a description of each step taken in accordance with subsection 21.1(2)`

-- s 21.1(2): reasonable steps (a) at least once during each financial year, (b) on the request of the
-- Director, and (c) at the times provided for in the regulations.
-- src:314 | (2) The corporation shall, at the following times, take reasonable steps to ensure that it has identified all individuals with significant control over the corporation and that the information in the register is accurate, complete and up-to-date:
-- src:315 | (a) at least once during each financial year of the corporation;
-- src:316 | (b) on the request of the Director; and
-- src:317 | (c) at the times provided for in the regulations.
@ref CBCA s 21.1(2) updating of information (src:314-317)
GIVEN `the corporation took reasonable steps during the financial year to ensure that it has identified all individuals with significant control and that the register is accurate, complete and up-to-date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Director requested that the steps be taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation took the steps on the request of the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a time is provided for in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the corporation took the steps at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation has taken the steps s 21.1(2) requires` MEANS
        `the corporation took reasonable steps during the financial year to ensure that it has identified all individuals with significant control and that the register is accurate, complete and up-to-date`
    AND (`the Director requested that the steps be taken` IMPLIES `the corporation took the steps on the request of the Director`)
    AND (`a time is provided for in the regulations` IMPLIES `the corporation took the steps at that time`)

-- s 21.1(3): record the information "within 15 days of becoming aware of it".
-- src:319 | (3) If the corporation becomes aware of any information referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) to (e) as a result of steps taken in accordance with subsection (2) or through any other means, the corporation shall record that information in the register within 15 days of becoming aware of it.
@ref CBCA s 21.1(3) recording of information (src:319)
DECIDE `the fifteen-day limit of s 21.1(3)` IS `Time limit` WITH
    `number of units` IS 15
    `unit of time` IS `calendar days`

-- src:319 | (3) If the corporation becomes aware of any information referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) to (e) as a result of steps taken in accordance with subsection (2) or through any other means, the corporation shall record that information in the register within 15 days of becoming aware of it.
@ref CBCA s 21.1(3) recording of information (src:319)
GIVEN `the day the corporation became aware of the information` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to record the information in the register within s 21.1(3)` MEANS
    `the last day of` `the fifteen-day limit of s 21.1(3)` `counted from` `the day the corporation became aware of the information`

-- src:319 | (3) If the corporation becomes aware of any information referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) to (e) as a result of steps taken in accordance with subsection (2) or through any other means, the corporation shall record that information in the register within 15 days of becoming aware of it.
@ref CBCA s 21.1(3) recording of information (src:319)
GIVEN `the day the corporation became aware of the information` IS A DATE
      `the day the corporation recorded the information in the register` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation recorded the information in time within s 21.1(3)` MEANS
    `done within the time limit` `the fifteen-day limit of s 21.1(3)` `the day the corporation became aware of the information` `the day the corporation recorded the information in the register`

-- s 21.1(4): a shareholder asked for information "shall, to the best of their knowledge, reply accurately and
-- completely as soon as feasible".
-- src:321 | (4) If the corporation requests information referred to in any of paragraphs (1)(a) to (e) from one of its shareholders, the shareholder shall, to the best of their knowledge, reply accurately and completely as soon as feasible.
@ref CBCA s 21.1(4) information from shareholders (src:321)
GIVEN `the corporation requested information referred to in paragraphs 21.1(1)(a) to (e) from the shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shareholder replied accurately and completely, to the best of their knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shareholder replied as soon as feasible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shareholder has complied with the duty to reply within s 21.1(4)` MEANS
    `the corporation requested information referred to in paragraphs 21.1(1)(a) to (e) from the shareholder`
    IMPLIES (    `the shareholder replied accurately and completely, to the best of their knowledge`
             AND `the shareholder replied as soon as feasible`)

-- s 21.1(5): "Within one year after the sixth anniversary of the day on which an individual ceases to be an
-- individual with significant control", dispose of that individual's personal information recorded in the
-- register, "subject to any other Act of Parliament and to any Act of the legislature of a province that
-- provides for a longer retention period". The date is NOTHING while the individual has not ceased, and
-- also where another Act provides a longer period: in that case that Act's period governs and this
-- subsection names no date.
-- src:323 | (5) Within one year after the sixth anniversary of the day on which an individual ceases to be an individual with significant control over the corporation, the corporation shall — subject to any other Act of Parliament and to any Act of the legislature of a province that provides for a longer retention period — dispose of any of that individual’s personal information, as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act, that is recorded in the register.
@ref CBCA s 21.1(5) disposal of personal information (src:323)
DECIDE `the six-year period of s 21.1(5)` IS `Time limit` WITH
    `number of units` IS 6
    `unit of time` IS `calendar years`

-- src:323 | (5) Within one year after the sixth anniversary of the day on which an individual ceases to be an individual with significant control over the corporation, the corporation shall — subject to any other Act of Parliament and to any Act of the legislature of a province that provides for a longer retention period — dispose of any of that individual’s personal information, as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act, that is recorded in the register.
@ref CBCA s 21.1(5) disposal of personal information (src:323)
DECIDE `the one-year period of s 21.1(5)` IS `Time limit` WITH
    `number of units` IS 1
    `unit of time` IS `calendar years`

-- src:323 | (5) Within one year after the sixth anniversary of the day on which an individual ceases to be an individual with significant control over the corporation, the corporation shall — subject to any other Act of Parliament and to any Act of the legislature of a province that provides for a longer retention period — dispose of any of that individual’s personal information, as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act, that is recorded in the register.
@ref CBCA s 21.1(5) disposal of personal information (src:323)
GIVEN `the day the individual ceased to be an individual with significant control` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `another Act provides for a longer retention period` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: other Acts of Parliament and provincial Acts (outside the Act)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day to dispose of the personal information within s 21.1(5)` MEANS
    IF `another Act provides for a longer retention period`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the day the individual ceased to be an individual with significant control`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST ceased THEN JUST (`the last day of` `the one-year period of s 21.1(5)` `counted from` (`the last day of` `the six-year period of s 21.1(5)` `counted from` ceased))

-- src:325 | (6) A corporation that, without reasonable cause, contravenes this section is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding $100,000.
@ref CBCA s 21.1(6) offence (src:325)
GIVEN `the corporation contravenes section 21.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation is guilty of an offence within s 21.1(6)` MEANS
        `the corporation contravenes section 21.1`
    AND (NOT `the corporation has reasonable cause`)

-- src:325 | (6) A corporation that, without reasonable cause, contravenes this section is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding $100,000.
@ref CBCA s 21.1(6) offence (src:325)
GIVETH A `Maximum punishment for an offence in Parts I to VI`
`the most a court may impose on summary conviction within s 21.1(6)` MEANS
    `Maximum punishment for an offence in Parts I to VI` WITH
        `maximum fine in dollars` IS 100000
        `maximum imprisonment in months` IS NOTHING

-- s 21.1(7): the section does not apply to a corporation (a) that is a reporting issuer, (b) any of whose
-- securities are listed and posted for trading on a designated stock exchange, or (c) that is a member of a
-- prescribed class. Sections 21.2, 21.21, 21.3 and 21.31 speak of "a corporation to which section 21.1
-- applies": this is that corporation.
-- src:327 | (7) This section does not apply to a corporation
-- src:328 | (a) that is a reporting issuer or an émetteur assujetti under an Act of the legislature of a province relating to the regulation of securities;
-- src:329 | (b) any of the securities of which are listed and posted for trading on a designated stock exchange, as defined in subsection 248(1) of the Income Tax Act; or
-- src:330 | (c) that is a member of a prescribed class.
@ref CBCA s 21.1(7) non-application (src:327-330)
GIVEN `the corporation is a reporting issuer or an émetteur assujetti under an Act of the legislature of a province relating to the regulation of securities` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: provincial securities Acts (outside the Act)
      `any of the securities of the corporation are listed and posted for trading on a designated stock exchange, as defined in subsection 248(1) of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 248(1) of the Income Tax Act (outside the Act)
      `the corporation is a member of a prescribed class` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 21.1 applies to the corporation within s 21.1(7)` MEANS
    NOT (    `the corporation is a reporting issuer or an émetteur assujetti under an Act of the legislature of a province relating to the regulation of securities`
          OR `any of the securities of the corporation are listed and posted for trading on a designated stock exchange, as defined in subsection 248(1) of the Income Tax Act`
          OR `the corporation is a member of a prescribed class`)

§§ `s 21.2 and s 21.21 inability to identify; sending information to the Director`

-- src:332 | 21.2 A corporation to which section 21.1 applies shall take prescribed steps if it is unable to identify any individuals with significant control over the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 21.2 inability to identify individuals (src:332)
GIVEN `section 21.1 applies to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is unable to identify any individuals with significant control over it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation took the prescribed steps` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation has complied with the duty to take prescribed steps within s 21.2` MEANS
    (    `section 21.1 applies to the corporation`
     AND `the corporation is unable to identify any individuals with significant control over it`)
    IMPLIES `the corporation took the prescribed steps`

-- src:334 | 21.21 (1) A corporation to which section 21.1 applies shall send to the Director
-- src:335 | (a) on an annual basis, the information determined by the Director from among that in its register of individuals with significant control over the corporation, in the form and within the period that the Director fixes; and
@ref CBCA s 21.21(1)(a) sending of information to Director (src:334-335)
GIVEN `section 21.1 applies to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation sent the Director, on an annual basis, the information the Director determined, in the form and within the period that the Director fixes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation has sent the annual information within s 21.21(1)(a)` MEANS
    `section 21.1 applies to the corporation`
    IMPLIES `the corporation sent the Director, on an annual basis, the information the Director determined, in the form and within the period that the Director fixes`

-- src:334 | 21.21 (1) A corporation to which section 21.1 applies shall send to the Director
-- src:336 | (b) the information determined by the Director from among that recorded under subsection 21.1(3), within 15 days after the day on which it is recorded and in the form that the Director fixes.
@ref CBCA s 21.21(1)(b) sending of information to Director (src:334 src:336)
DECIDE `the fifteen-day limit of s 21.21(1)(b)` IS `Time limit` WITH
    `number of units` IS 15
    `unit of time` IS `calendar days`

-- src:334 | 21.21 (1) A corporation to which section 21.1 applies shall send to the Director
-- src:336 | (b) the information determined by the Director from among that recorded under subsection 21.1(3), within 15 days after the day on which it is recorded and in the form that the Director fixes.
@ref CBCA s 21.21(1)(b) sending of information to Director (src:334 src:336)
GIVEN `the day the information was recorded under subsection 21.1(3)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to send the recorded information to the Director within s 21.21(1)(b)` MEANS
    `the last day of` `the fifteen-day limit of s 21.21(1)(b)` `counted from` `the day the information was recorded under subsection 21.1(3)`

-- src:334 | 21.21 (1) A corporation to which section 21.1 applies shall send to the Director
-- src:336 | (b) the information determined by the Director from among that recorded under subsection 21.1(3), within 15 days after the day on which it is recorded and in the form that the Director fixes.
@ref CBCA s 21.21(1)(b) sending of information to Director (src:334 src:336)
GIVEN `section 21.1 applies to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the information was recorded under subsection 21.1(3)` IS A DATE
      `the day the corporation sent the information to the Director` IS A DATE
      `the information was sent in the form that the Director fixes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation has sent the recorded information in time within s 21.21(1)(b)` MEANS
    `section 21.1 applies to the corporation`
    IMPLIES (    `done within the time limit` `the fifteen-day limit of s 21.21(1)(b)` `the day the information was recorded under subsection 21.1(3)` `the day the corporation sent the information to the Director`
             AND `the information was sent in the form that the Director fixes`)

-- s 21.21(2): "On or after the date shown on a certificate referred to in section 8 or subsection 185(4) or
-- 187(4)", the corporation sends the information determined by the Director from among that in paragraphs
-- 21.1(1)(a) to (f), in the form and within the period the Director fixes.
-- src:338 | (2) On or after the date shown on a certificate referred to in section 8 or subsection 185(4) or 187(4), a corporation to which section 21.1 applies shall send to the Director the information determined by the Director from among that referred to in paragraphs 21.1(1)(a) to (f), in the form and within the period that the Director fixes.
@ref CBCA s 21.21(2) certificates issued (src:338)
GIVEN `section 21.1 applies to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date shown on a certificate referred to in section 8 or subsection 185(4) or 187(4)` IS A DATE   -- out of range: sections 185(4) and 187(4) (piece cb4)
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the duty to send information to the Director has arisen within s 21.21(2)` MEANS
        `section 21.1 applies to the corporation`
    AND day AT LEAST `the date shown on a certificate referred to in section 8 or subsection 185(4) or 187(4)`

-- src:338 | (2) On or after the date shown on a certificate referred to in section 8 or subsection 185(4) or 187(4), a corporation to which section 21.1 applies shall send to the Director the information determined by the Director from among that referred to in paragraphs 21.1(1)(a) to (f), in the form and within the period that the Director fixes.
@ref CBCA s 21.21(2) certificates issued (src:338)
GIVEN `the duty to send information to the Director has arisen under subsection 21.21(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation sent the information the Director determined, in the form and within the period that the Director fixes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation has complied with the duty to send information on a certificate within s 21.21(2)` MEANS
    `the duty to send information to the Director has arisen under subsection 21.21(2)`
    IMPLIES `the corporation sent the information the Director determined, in the form and within the period that the Director fixes`

-- s 21.21(3): the Director "is not required to keep or produce any information ... after the end of the
-- six-year period following the day on which it is received".
-- src:340 | (3) The Director is not required to keep or produce any information received under subsection (1) or (2) after the end of the six-year period following the day on which it is received.
@ref CBCA s 21.21(3) period for keeping and producing information (src:340)
DECIDE `the six-year period of s 21.21(3)` IS `Time limit` WITH
    `number of units` IS 6
    `unit of time` IS `calendar years`

-- src:340 | (3) The Director is not required to keep or produce any information received under subsection (1) or (2) after the end of the six-year period following the day on which it is received.
@ref CBCA s 21.21(3) period for keeping and producing information (src:340)
GIVEN `the day the Director received the information` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director is required to keep or produce the information on the day within s 21.21(3)` MEANS
    `done within the time limit` `the six-year period of s 21.21(3)` `the day the Director received the information` day

-- src:342 | (4) A corporation that, without reasonable cause, contravenes subsection (1) or (2) is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding $100,000.
