        `maximum imprisonment in months` IS NOTHING

§§ `s 21.3 disclosure to the Director`

-- Subsections (2) to (6) are repealed in this text (src:345-349).
-- src:344 | 21.3 (1) A corporation to which section 21.1 applies shall disclose to the Director, on request, any information in its register of individuals with significant control.
@ref CBCA s 21.3(1) disclosure to Director (src:344)
GIVEN `section 21.1 applies to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Director has requested the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must disclose the information in its register to the Director within s 21.3(1)` MEANS
        `section 21.1 applies to the corporation`
    AND `the Director has requested the disclosure`

§§ `s 21.301 to s 21.303 what the Director may provide and must publish`

-- s 21.301 and s 21.302: the Director "may provide all or part of the information received under section
-- 21.21" to the recipients they name. Whether the Director does is the Director's choice: the rule says
-- whether the Director may.
-- src:351 | 21.301 The Director may provide all or part of the information received under section 21.21 to an investigative body referred to in subsection 21.31(2), the Financial Transactions and Reports Analysis Centre of Canada or any prescribed entity.
-- src:353 | 21.302 The Director may provide all or part of the information received under section 21.21 to a provincial corporate registry or a provincial government department or agency that is responsible for corporate law in that province.
@ref CBCA s 21.301, s 21.302 provision of information by Director (src:351 src:353)
DECLARE `Recipient of information from the Director (s 21.301, s 21.302)` IS ONE OF
    `an investigative body referred to in subsection 21.31(2)`
    `the Financial Transactions and Reports Analysis Centre of Canada`
    `a prescribed entity`
    `a provincial corporate registry`
    `a provincial government department or agency that is responsible for corporate law in that province`
    `any other recipient`

-- src:351 | 21.301 The Director may provide all or part of the information received under section 21.21 to an investigative body referred to in subsection 21.31(2), the Financial Transactions and Reports Analysis Centre of Canada or any prescribed entity.
-- src:353 | 21.302 The Director may provide all or part of the information received under section 21.21 to a provincial corporate registry or a provincial government department or agency that is responsible for corporate law in that province.
@ref CBCA s 21.301, s 21.302 provision of information by Director (src:351 src:353)
GIVEN recipient IS A `Recipient of information from the Director (s 21.301, s 21.302)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director may provide the information received under section 21.21 to the recipient within s 21.301 and s 21.302` MEANS
    CONSIDER recipient
    WHEN `an investigative body referred to in subsection 21.31(2)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Financial Transactions and Reports Analysis Centre of Canada` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a prescribed entity` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a provincial corporate registry` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a provincial government department or agency that is responsible for corporate law in that province` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other recipient` THEN FALSE

-- s 21.303(1): what the Director "shall make available to the public" for each individual with significant
-- control; (2): not for an individual under 18 or to whom prescribed circumstances apply; (3): the Director
-- "may choose to not make it available" on application, in the cases listed.
-- src:355 | 21.303 (1) The Director shall make available to the public the following information sent to the Director under section 21.21 for each individual with significant control:
-- src:356 | (a) their name;
-- src:357 | (b) their address for service, if it has been provided to the corporation;
-- src:358 | (c) their residential address, if their address for service has not been provided to the corporation;
-- src:359 | (d) the information referred to in paragraphs 21.1(1)(c) and (d); and
-- src:360 | (e) any other prescribed information.
@ref CBCA s 21.303(1) information available to public (src:355-360)
DECLARE `Item of information about an individual with significant control (s 21.303(1))` IS ONE OF
    `their name`
    `their address for service`
    `their residential address`
    `the day they became or ceased to be an individual with significant control, or a description of how they are one (paragraphs 21.1(1)(c) and (d))`
    `other prescribed information`
    `any other item`

-- src:355 | 21.303 (1) The Director shall make available to the public the following information sent to the Director under section 21.21 for each individual with significant control:
-- src:356 | (a) their name;
-- src:357 | (b) their address for service, if it has been provided to the corporation;
-- src:358 | (c) their residential address, if their address for service has not been provided to the corporation;
-- src:359 | (d) the information referred to in paragraphs 21.1(1)(c) and (d); and
-- src:360 | (e) any other prescribed information.
-- src:362 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply in respect of an individual who is less than 18 years of age or an individual to whom prescribed circumstances apply.
-- src:364 | (3) If an individual with significant control or the corporation over which they have significant control applies to the Director to have any information referred to in subsection (1) in relation to the individual not made available to the public, the Director may choose to not make it available to the public, subject to any terms that the Director thinks fit,
@ref CBCA s 21.303(1), s 21.303(2), s 21.303(3) information available to public (src:355-360 src:362 src:364)
GIVEN item IS AN `Item of information about an individual with significant control (s 21.303(1))`
      `their address for service has been provided to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is less than 18 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `prescribed circumstances apply to the individual` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the Director has chosen not to make the information available under subsection 21.303(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director must make the item available to the public within s 21.303` MEANS
        (CONSIDER item
         WHEN `their name` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `their address for service` THEN `their address for service has been provided to the corporation`
         WHEN `their residential address` THEN NOT `their address for service has been provided to the corporation`
         WHEN `the day they became or ceased to be an individual with significant control, or a description of how they are one (paragraphs 21.1(1)(c) and (d))` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `other prescribed information` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `any other item` THEN FALSE)
    AND (NOT `the individual is less than 18 years of age`)
    AND (NOT `prescribed circumstances apply to the individual`)
    AND (NOT `the Director has chosen not to make the information available under subsection 21.303(3)`)

-- src:364 | (3) If an individual with significant control or the corporation over which they have significant control applies to the Director to have any information referred to in subsection (1) in relation to the individual not made available to the public, the Director may choose to not make it available to the public, subject to any terms that the Director thinks fit,
-- src:365 | (a) if the Director reasonably believes that making it available presents or would present a serious threat to the safety of the individual; or
-- src:366 | (b) if the Director is satisfied that
-- src:367 | (i) the individual is incapable,
-- src:368 | (ii) the information is to be kept confidential under subsection 27(8) of the Conflict of Interest Act or a similar provision of an Act of the legislature of a province, or
-- src:369 | (iii) prescribed circumstances apply to the individual.
@ref CBCA s 21.303(3) exemption on application (src:364-369)
GIVEN `the individual with significant control or the corporation over which they have significant control has applied to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Director reasonably believes that making the information available presents or would present a serious threat to the safety of the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Director is satisfied that the individual is incapable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Director is satisfied that the information is to be kept confidential under subsection 27(8) of the Conflict of Interest Act or a similar provision of an Act of the legislature of a province` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 27(8) of the Conflict of Interest Act (outside the Act)
      `the Director is satisfied that prescribed circumstances apply to the individual` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director may choose not to make the information available to the public within s 21.303(3)` MEANS
        `the individual with significant control or the corporation over which they have significant control has applied to the Director`
    AND (    `the Director reasonably believes that making the information available presents or would present a serious threat to the safety of the individual`
          OR `the Director is satisfied that the individual is incapable`
          OR `the Director is satisfied that the information is to be kept confidential under subsection 27(8) of the Conflict of Interest Act or a similar provision of an Act of the legislature of a province`
          OR `the Director is satisfied that prescribed circumstances apply to the individual`)

§§ `s 21.31 and s 21.32 requests by investigative bodies`

-- src:375 | (2) The investigative bodies for the purpose of this section are
-- src:376 | (a) any police force;
-- src:377 | (b) the Canada Revenue Agency and any provincial body that has responsibilities similar to those of the Canada Revenue Agency; and
-- src:378 | (c) any prescribed body that has investigative powers in relation to offences referred to in the schedule.
@ref CBCA s 21.31(2) investigative bodies (src:375-378)
DECLARE `Investigative body (s 21.31(2))` IS ONE OF
    `a police force`
    `the Canada Revenue Agency`
    `a provincial body that has responsibilities similar to those of the Canada Revenue Agency`
    `a prescribed body that has investigative powers in relation to offences referred to in the schedule`
    `any other body`

-- src:375 | (2) The investigative bodies for the purpose of this section are
-- src:376 | (a) any police force;
-- src:377 | (b) the Canada Revenue Agency and any provincial body that has responsibilities similar to those of the Canada Revenue Agency; and
-- src:378 | (c) any prescribed body that has investigative powers in relation to offences referred to in the schedule.
@ref CBCA s 21.31(2) investigative bodies (src:375-378)
GIVEN body IS AN `Investigative body (s 21.31(2))`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the body is an investigative body for the purpose of s 21.31 within s 21.31(2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER body
    WHEN `a police force` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Canada Revenue Agency` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a provincial body that has responsibilities similar to those of the Canada Revenue Agency` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a prescribed body that has investigative powers in relation to offences referred to in the schedule` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other body` THEN FALSE

-- s 21.31(1): on request by an investigative body, a corporation to which s 21.1 applies shall, as soon as
-- feasible after the request is served or deemed received, provide a copy of the register or disclose the
-- specified information. Subsection (3) limits when the body "may make a request"; the corporation's duty
-- in (1) is stated to arise "on request by an investigative body referred to in subsection (2)" and not on
-- a request that meets (3) (fork cb1-F5 in NOTES.md).
-- src:371 | 21.31 (1) On request by an investigative body referred to in subsection (2), a corporation to which section 21.1 applies shall, as soon as feasible after the request is served on the corporation or deemed to be received by it, and in the manner specified by the investigative body,
-- src:375 | (2) The investigative bodies for the purpose of this section are
-- src:376 | (a) any police force;
-- src:377 | (b) the Canada Revenue Agency and any provincial body that has responsibilities similar to those of the Canada Revenue Agency; and
-- src:378 | (c) any prescribed body that has investigative powers in relation to offences referred to in the schedule.
@ref CBCA s 21.31(1), s 21.31(2) disclosure to investigative bodies (src:371 src:375-378)
GIVEN body IS AN `Investigative body (s 21.31(2))`
      `section 21.1 applies to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request has been served on the corporation or is deemed to be received by it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must provide the copy of its register or disclose the specified information within s 21.31(1)` MEANS
        `section 21.1 applies to the corporation`
    AND `the body is an investigative body for the purpose of s 21.31 within s 21.31(2)` body
    AND `the request has been served on the corporation or is deemed to be received by it`

-- s 21.31(3): "may make a request only if it has reasonable grounds to suspect" that the copy or information
-- would be relevant to investigating an offence in the schedule "and it also has reasonable grounds to
-- suspect" one of three further things.
-- src:380 | (3) An investigative body may make a request only if it has reasonable grounds to suspect that the copy of the register or the specified information would be relevant to investigating an offence referred to in the schedule and it also has reasonable grounds to suspect that
-- src:381 | (a) the corporation that is the subject of the request committed the offence or was used to
-- src:382 | (i) commit the offence,
-- src:383 | (ii) facilitate the commission of the offence, or
-- src:384 | (iii) protect from detection or punishment a person who has committed the offence;
-- src:385 | (b) an individual with significant control over the corporation that is the subject of the request is also an individual with significant control over a corporation that committed the offence or was used to do anything referred to in any of subparagraphs (a)(i) to (iii); or
-- src:386 | (c) an individual with significant control over the corporation that is the subject of the request is also an individual who, directly or indirectly, influences the affairs of an entity, other than a corporation, that committed the offence or was used to do anything referred to in any of subparagraphs (a)(i) to (iii).
@ref CBCA s 21.31(3) requirement (src:380-386)
GIVEN `the body has reasonable grounds to suspect that the copy of the register or the specified information would be relevant to investigating an offence referred to in the schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body has reasonable grounds to suspect that the corporation committed the offence or was used to commit it, to facilitate its commission or to protect from detection or punishment a person who has committed it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body has reasonable grounds to suspect that an individual with significant control over the corporation is also an individual with significant control over a corporation that committed the offence or was used to do any of those things` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body has reasonable grounds to suspect that an individual with significant control over the corporation is also an individual who, directly or indirectly, influences the affairs of an entity other than a corporation that committed the offence or was used to do any of those things` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the investigative body may make the request within s 21.31(3)` MEANS
        `the body has reasonable grounds to suspect that the copy of the register or the specified information would be relevant to investigating an offence referred to in the schedule`
    AND (    `the body has reasonable grounds to suspect that the corporation committed the offence or was used to commit it, to facilitate its commission or to protect from detection or punishment a person who has committed it`
          OR `the body has reasonable grounds to suspect that an individual with significant control over the corporation is also an individual with significant control over a corporation that committed the offence or was used to do any of those things`
          OR `the body has reasonable grounds to suspect that an individual with significant control over the corporation is also an individual who, directly or indirectly, influences the affairs of an entity other than a corporation that committed the offence or was used to do any of those things`)

-- s 21.31(4): served by leaving the request at the registered office as shown in the last notice filed under
-- section 19, or sent by registered mail to that office and, if so sent, deemed received when it would be
-- delivered in the ordinary course of mail, unless there are reasonable grounds for believing the
-- corporation did not receive it at that time or at all. A request left at the office is served that day.
-- NOTHING: the text names no day (not yet left or sent, or reasonable grounds for believing it did not
-- arrive, in which case receipt is a question of fact for the court).
-- src:388 | (4) The request must be served on the corporation by leaving the request at the corporation’s registered office as shown in the last notice filed under section 19 or sent to the corporation by registered mail to that registered office and, if so sent, is deemed to be received at the time it would be delivered in the ordinary course of mail, unless there are reasonable grounds for believing that the corporation did not receive the request at that time or at all.
@ref CBCA s 21.31(4) service or sending of request (src:388)
GIVEN `the day the request was left at the registered office` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the request would be delivered in the ordinary course of mail if sent by registered mail to the registered office` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `there are reasonable grounds for believing that the corporation did not receive the request at that time or at all` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day the request is served or deemed received within s 21.31(4)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the request was left at the registered office`
    WHEN JUST left THEN JUST left
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER `the day the request would be delivered in the ordinary course of mail if sent by registered mail to the registered office`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST delivered THEN
            IF `there are reasonable grounds for believing that the corporation did not receive the request at that time or at all`
            THEN NOTHING
            ELSE JUST delivered

-- src:390 | (5) A corporation that, without reasonable cause, contravenes subsection (1) is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine of not more than $100,000.
@ref CBCA s 21.31(5) offence (src:390)
GIVEN `the corporation contravenes subsection 21.31(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation is guilty of an offence within s 21.31(5)` MEANS
        `the corporation contravenes subsection 21.31(1)`
    AND (NOT `the corporation has reasonable cause`)

-- src:390 | (5) A corporation that, without reasonable cause, contravenes subsection (1) is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine of not more than $100,000.
@ref CBCA s 21.31(5) offence (src:390)
GIVETH A `Maximum punishment for an offence in Parts I to VI`
`the most a court may impose on summary conviction within s 21.31(5)` MEANS
    `Maximum punishment for an offence in Parts I to VI` WITH
        `maximum fine in dollars` IS 100000
        `maximum imprisonment in months` IS NOTHING

-- s 21.32(1): the record an investigative body keeps of a request it makes.
-- src:394 | 21.32 (1) Every investigative body that makes a request under subsection 21.31(1) shall keep a record setting out the following:
-- src:395 | (a) the name of the corporation that was the subject of the request;
-- src:396 | (b) the reasonable grounds on which the request was based;
-- src:397 | (c) information respecting what was requested;
-- src:398 | (d) the date the request was served or deemed to have been received;
-- src:399 | (e) information respecting the service or the sending of the request;
-- src:400 | (f) all information received from the corporation in response to the request; and
-- src:401 | (g) any prescribed information.
@ref CBCA s 21.32(1) record (src:394-401)
DECLARE `Record kept by an investigative body of a request (s 21.32(1))` HAS
    `it sets out the name of the corporation that was the subject of the request` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it sets out the reasonable grounds on which the request was based` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it sets out information respecting what was requested` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it sets out the date the request was served or deemed to have been received` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it sets out information respecting the service or the sending of the request` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it sets out all information received from the corporation in response to the request` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is prescribed information` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
    `it sets out the prescribed information` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)

-- src:394 | 21.32 (1) Every investigative body that makes a request under subsection 21.31(1) shall keep a record setting out the following:
-- src:395 | (a) the name of the corporation that was the subject of the request;
-- src:396 | (b) the reasonable grounds on which the request was based;
-- src:397 | (c) information respecting what was requested;
-- src:398 | (d) the date the request was served or deemed to have been received;
-- src:399 | (e) information respecting the service or the sending of the request;
-- src:400 | (f) all information received from the corporation in response to the request; and
-- src:401 | (g) any prescribed information.
@ref CBCA s 21.32(1) record (src:394-401)
GIVEN record IS A `Record kept by an investigative body of a request (s 21.32(1))`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the investigative body has kept the record s 21.32(1) requires` MEANS
        record's `it sets out the name of the corporation that was the subject of the request`
    AND record's `it sets out the reasonable grounds on which the request was based`
    AND record's `it sets out information respecting what was requested`
    AND record's `it sets out the date the request was served or deemed to have been received`
    AND record's `it sets out information respecting the service or the sending of the request`
    AND record's `it sets out all information received from the corporation in response to the request`
    AND (record's `there is prescribed information` IMPLIES record's `it sets out the prescribed information`)

-- s 21.32(2): within 90 days after the end of the calendar year in which the request was made, a report to
-- the Director of the total number of requests and, for the RCMP and the CRA, the number in each province.
-- The text reads "after the end the calendar year" (sic); the year ends on 31 December.
-- src:403 | (2) Every investigative body that makes a request under subsection 21.31(1) shall, within 90 days after the end the calendar year in which the request was made, provide the Director with a report setting out the total number of requests made by it in that year and, in the case of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Canada Revenue Agency, the number of requests made in each province.
@ref CBCA s 21.32(2) report (src:403)
DECIDE `the ninety-day limit of s 21.32(2)` IS `Time limit` WITH
    `number of units` IS 90
    `unit of time` IS `calendar days`

-- src:403 | (2) Every investigative body that makes a request under subsection 21.31(1) shall, within 90 days after the end the calendar year in which the request was made, provide the Director with a report setting out the total number of requests made by it in that year and, in the case of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Canada Revenue Agency, the number of requests made in each province.
@ref CBCA s 21.32(2) report (src:403)
GIVEN `the calendar year in which the request was made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the investigative body to report to the Director within s 21.32(2)` MEANS
    `the last day of` `the ninety-day limit of s 21.32(2)` `counted from` (YMD `the calendar year in which the request was made` 12 31)

-- src:403 | (2) Every investigative body that makes a request under subsection 21.31(1) shall, within 90 days after the end the calendar year in which the request was made, provide the Director with a report setting out the total number of requests made by it in that year and, in the case of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Canada Revenue Agency, the number of requests made in each province.
@ref CBCA s 21.32(2) report (src:403)
GIVEN `the report sets out the total number of requests made by the body in that year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is the Royal Canadian Mounted Police or the Canada Revenue Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report sets out the number of requests made in each province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the investigative body's report has the contents s 21.32(2) requires` MEANS
        `the report sets out the total number of requests made by the body in that year`
    AND (`the body is the Royal Canadian Mounted Police or the Canada Revenue Agency` IMPLIES `the report sets out the number of requests made in each province`)

-- s 21.32(3): "Section 251 does not apply in respect of a contravention of subsection (1) or (2)." Whether
-- section 251 (out of range, piece cb5) applies to any other contravention is that section's own business,
-- so the answer for those is NOTHING.
-- src:405 | (3) Section 251 does not apply in respect of a contravention of subsection (1) or (2).
@ref CBCA s 21.32(3) non-application (src:405)
GIVEN `the contravention is of subsection 21.32(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 251 applies to the contravention within s 21.32(3)` MEANS
    IF `the contravention is of subsection 21.32(1) or (2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 21.4 offences`

-- (1): a director or officer who knowingly authorizes, permits or acquiesces in the corporation's
-- contravention commits an offence "whether or not the corporation has been prosecuted or convicted".
-- src:407 | 21.4 (1) Every director or officer of a corporation who knowingly authorizes, permits or acquiesces in the contravention of subsection 21.1(1), 21.21(1) or (2), 21.3(1) or 21.31(1) by that corporation commits an offence, whether or not the corporation has been prosecuted or convicted.
@ref CBCA s 21.4(1) offence (src:407)
GIVEN `the person is a director or officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation contravened subsection 21.1(1), 21.21(1) or (2), 21.3(1) or 21.31(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has been prosecuted or convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director or officer commits an offence within s 21.4(1)` MEANS
        `the person is a director or officer of the corporation`
    AND `the corporation contravened subsection 21.1(1), 21.21(1) or (2), 21.3(1) or 21.31(1)`
    AND `the person knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the contravention`

-- src:409 | (2) Every director or officer of a corporation who knowingly records or knowingly authorizes, permits or acquiesces in the recording of false or misleading information in the register of the corporation referred to in subsection 21.1(1) commits an offence.
@ref CBCA s 21.4(2) offence -- recording of false or misleading information (src:409)
GIVEN `the person is a director or officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly recorded, or knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the recording of, false or misleading information in the register of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director or officer commits an offence within s 21.4(2)` MEANS
        `the person is a director or officer of the corporation`
    AND `the person knowingly recorded, or knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the recording of, false or misleading information in the register of the corporation`

-- src:411 | (3) Every director or officer of a corporation who knowingly provides or knowingly authorizes, permits or acquiesces in the provision to any person or entity of false or misleading information in relation to the register of the corporation referred to in subsection 21.1(1) commits an offence.
@ref CBCA s 21.4(3) offence -- provision of false or misleading information (src:411)
GIVEN `the person is a director or officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly provided, or knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the provision to any person or entity of, false or misleading information in relation to the register of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director or officer commits an offence within s 21.4(3)` MEANS
        `the person is a director or officer of the corporation`
    AND `the person knowingly provided, or knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the provision to any person or entity of, false or misleading information in relation to the register of the corporation`

-- src:413 | (4) Every shareholder who knowingly contravenes subsection 21.1(4) commits an offence.
@ref CBCA s 21.4(4) offence -- subsection 21.1(4) (src:413)
GIVEN `the person is a shareholder of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shareholder knowingly contravened subsection 21.1(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shareholder commits an offence within s 21.4(4)` MEANS
        `the person is a shareholder of the corporation`
    AND `the shareholder knowingly contravened subsection 21.1(4)`

-- src:415 | (5) A person who commits an offence under any of subsections (1) to (4) is liable
-- src:416 | (a) on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding $200,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years, or to both; or
-- src:417 | (b) on conviction on indictment, to a fine not exceeding $1,000,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years, or to both.
@ref CBCA s 21.4(5) offence (src:415-417)
DECLARE `Mode of prosecution (s 21.4(5))` IS ONE OF
    `summary conviction`
    `conviction on indictment`

-- "(a) on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding $200,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- two years, or to both; or (b) on conviction on indictment, to a fine not exceeding $1,000,000 or to
-- imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years, or to both."
-- src:415 | (5) A person who commits an offence under any of subsections (1) to (4) is liable
-- src:416 | (a) on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding $200,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years, or to both; or
-- src:417 | (b) on conviction on indictment, to a fine not exceeding $1,000,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years, or to both.
@ref CBCA s 21.4(5) offence (src:415-417)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of prosecution (s 21.4(5))`
GIVETH A `Maximum punishment for an offence in Parts I to VI`
`the most a court may impose within s 21.4(5)` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `summary conviction` THEN
        `Maximum punishment for an offence in Parts I to VI` WITH
            `maximum fine in dollars` IS 200000
            `maximum imprisonment in months` IS JUST 24
    WHEN `conviction on indictment` THEN
        `Maximum punishment for an offence in Parts I to VI` WITH
            `maximum fine in dollars` IS 1000000
            `maximum imprisonment in months` IS JUST 60
